ain separately authorized backend credentials through a trusted issuer or supported exchange. Never accept a token for another resource or relay it unchanged as a substitute for backend authorization. Keep backend secrets and tokens away from agent-controlled execution paths. Restrict local process launch, files, environment, credentials, and network in the host or sandbox. Under MCP 2026-07-28, reject metadata-header/body mismatches before routing or policy relies on them. Isolate private caches by verified authorization context, tenant, resource, and policy version; share only data explicitly approved as public. Authorize explicit task/state handles on every operation; neither a connection nor \nE07 {\"gate\": \"G2\", \"title\": \"Untrusted peer messages\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message, even validly signed ones. Validate message types and schemas, and check what that peer is allowed to ask for. Where a replay could repeat an action, check freshness and track nonces or request IDs. Checking the sender alone doesn't stop replays. Test faked identity, replayed requests, requests across tenants, and instructions passed along by a compromised peer. Verify signed agent cards where they exist. A card says who an agent is, not what it may do. Check callback and webhook URLs against SSRF. A valid sender doesn't make a message's content trusted.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Tool server identified only by its self-reported name\", \"owner\": \"E05\"}, {\"problem\": \"Missing schema or size checks on API responses\", \"owner\": \"R01\"}, {\"problem\": \"Peers or children still running after a stop\", \"owner\": \"E09\"}, {\"problem\": \"Run can't be rebuilt across gateway, tool services, and delegated workers\", \"owner\": \"E10\"}], \"na_when\": \"The agent receives no messages from other agents (no A2A server, peer endpoint, or agent-to-agent channel).\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E07.1\", \"check\": \"Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is aut\nE08 {\"gate\": \"G1\", \"title\": \"Bounded delegated authority\", \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\", \"requirement\": \"Give sub-agents only the powers approved for their task. Preserve the verified original subject and current actor through each handoff and enforce their task, tenant, resource, and audience limits where the action runs. Use supported token exchange or narrow task credentials rather than copying a parent's full credential. A parent must not gain a denied power by asking a more powerful peer to act without separate valid approval. For RFC 8693 tokens, earlier nested actors are provenance only and never add access. An actor chain or signed identity does not prove that a requested action was approved. Test legitimate delegation and that escalation attempt.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Approvals that can be replayed or aren't tied to exact arguments\", \"owner\": \"B06\"}, {\"problem\": \"Prompt a parent gave a sub-agent not recorded\", \"owner\": \"A06\"}, {\"problem\": \"Children still running after the parent is stopped\", \"owner\": \"E09\"}, {\"problem\": \"Replayed or faked peer-agent messages\", \"owner\": \"E07\"}, {\"problem\": \"No limit on how many sub-agents a run can start\", \"owner\": \"B07\"}], \"na_when\": \"The agent never delegates to sub-agents or peer agents.\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E08.1\", \"check\": \"Each child gets a credential narrowed to its approved task (for example by token exchange or transaction tokens), never the parent's full credential.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where a c\nE09 {\"gate\": \"G1\", \"title\": \"Recursive shutdown\", \"lead_role\": \"operations\", \"requirement\": \"Run a drill across a parent, nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks, where they exist. Check that the stop reaches every descendant within the set time. It must revoke access as needed and prevent orphaned retries or restarts. Record how outside effects that already happened are reconciled.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"Agent able to disable or delay its own stop\", \"owner\": \"R11\"}, {\"problem\": \"No way to cut off the agent's access without cutting off the user\", \"owner\": \"B04\"}, {\"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type\", \"owner\": \"E12\"}, {\"problem\": \"Sub-agent given powers beyond its task\", \"owner\": \"E08\"}], \"na_when\": \"never\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E09.1\", \"check\": \"A stop signal from the root reaches every descendant: nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the stop handler. 2) Check it reaches nested children, remote workers, queued jobs, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks (cancel calls, MCP `notifications/cancelled`). 3) Answer no if any of these that exists in the code is not reached, or stop only sets an in-process flag that remote workers never read.\"}, {\"id\": \"E09.2\", \"check\": \"Stopping revokes descendants' credentials or leases, and leases or tokens are short-lived, so a disconnected worker\n{'brace_checklist': '2026-10-01', 'repo': '', 'commit': None, 'reviewed_at': '2026-10-20T12:49:56Z', 'scope': \"TODO: what was reviewed and what wasn't.\", 'review_protocol': 'coverage-first-v1', 'findings': ['E05', 'E06', 'E07', 'E08', 'E09'], 'injection_attempts': [], 'prescan_resolutions': {}}\n./infra/terraform/main.tf\n./infra/terraform/github.tf\n./infra/terraform/iam.tf\n./test/controls.test.ts\n./test/budget.test.ts\n./config/tools.allowlist.yaml\n./config/policy.yaml\n./config/budgets.yaml\n./Dockerfile\n./k8s/deployment.yaml\n./release/manifest.json\n./brace-findings.json\n./README.md\n./package.json\n./.github/CODEOWNERS\n./.github/workflows/deploy.yml\n./.github/workflows/ci.yml\n./prompts/intent-classifier.txt\n./prompts/system.md\n./tsconfig.json\n./src/tools/executor.ts\n./src/tools/metadata-scan.ts\n./src/tools/registry.ts\n./src/tools/approvals.ts\n./src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts\n./src/agent/identity.ts\n./src/agent/context-size.ts\n./src/agent/loop.ts\n./src/agent/budget.ts\n./src/agent/classifier.ts\n./src/integrations/sms.ts\n./src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts\n./src/integrations/payments.ts\n./src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts\n./src/audit/recorder.ts\n./src/workers/reminders.ts\n./src/config.ts\n./src/server.ts\n./src/routes/webchat.ts\n./src/routes/sms-webhook.ts\n./src/control/kill-switch.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016uDexzBNS61aKbFc8EMZ4j","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
