{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDWzsyDE75eYdEX3VDvy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FBUmx23nbwfVwekTGTqEe8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-499x1leg && PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; $PY -c \"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('batch-policy.json'))\nfor k in d:\n  print('=====',k,d[k]['requirement'][:3000]);\n  for c in d[k]['checks']: print(json.dumps(c))\n\"; for c in E05.1 E05.2 E05.3 E05.4; do $PY skill/scripts/review_coverage.py policy $c --repo agent; done 2>&1 | head -80"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15271,"cache_read_input_tokens":26358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15271},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c4b6767-3afe-4fbc-ad1e-9f5c27d75379","uuid":"56d1e473-71ba-4467-a03c-10fd4efba1bf","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:50:30.159Z","request_id":"req_011CgDWzsgrCBpuEnCBvRVxs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FBUmx23nbwfVwekTGTqEe8":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-499x1leg && PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; $PY -c \"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('batch-policy.json'))\nfor k in d:\n  print('=====',k,d[k]['requirement'][:3000]);\n  for c in d[k]['checks']: print(json.dumps(c))\n\"; for c in E05.1 E05.2 E05.3 E05.4; do $PY skill/scripts/review_coverage.py policy $c --repo agent; done 2>&1 | head -80"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FBUmx23nbwfVwekTGTqEe8","type":"tool_result","content":"===== E05 Identify each tool by a verified server identity plus the tool name. Base server identity on the verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace. A server's self-reported name is neither unique nor trustworthy. Flag lookalike and duplicate names across servers. Test that a new server can't quietly swap its tool in for an approved one.\n{\"id\": \"E05.1\", \"check\": \"Tools are keyed by verified server identity (endpoint, credential, or registry namespace) plus tool name, never by bare tool name or a server's self-reported name.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the tool registry or lookup map. 2) Check its key is a verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace plus tool name. 3) Answer no if tools are keyed by bare tool name or the server's self-reported name (`serverInfo.name`), or a later server overwrites an earlier entry with the same tool name.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E05.2\", \"check\": \"The registry flags duplicate and lookalike tool names across servers.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"attempt_categories\": [\"repeated_confusables\", \"multiple_edits\", \"normalization_boundary\"], \"verify\": \"1) Trace name comparison across servers. 2) Construct repeated confusable substitutions, multiple edits and normalization-boundary examples, starting from an existing tool name; record canonical outputs, comparison result and registration outcome. 3) Answer no if a duplicate or demonstrated lookalike is accepted without a conflict flag. The existence of normalization/edit-distance code is insufficient; namespacing and approval binding do not satisfy this separate check.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E05.3\", \"check\": \"Approval is bound to the verified server identity, so a new server with a matching tool name or self-reported name does not inherit approval or replace the approved tool.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where tool approval is stored and checked. 2) Check approval is keyed by verified server identity, not tool name or self-reported server name. 3) Answer no if a new server with a matching tool name or server name would count as approved or replace the approved tool.\"}\n===== E06 Send MCP calls through a gateway or equivalent enforcement layer the agent cannot bypass. Choose controls for internal HTTP servers, public third-party services, and local stdio servers; private networking and mTLS are one internal deployment pattern, not universal MCP requirements. Authenticate each caller, preserve agent and delegated-subject identity, and authorize each action's tool, operation, resource, tenant, and arguments. Apply the same policy to direct calls, dynamic tools, CLI/code mode, and wrappers. Validate calls and responses, enforce rate limits, and log every decision. For HTTP OAuth, validate access tokens for the gateway's own audience, issuer, expiry, and scopes; obtain separately authorized backend credentials through a trusted issuer or supported exchange. Never accept a token for another resource or relay it unchanged as a substitute for backend authorization. Keep backend secrets and tokens away from agent-controlled execution paths. Restrict local process launch, files, environment, credentials, and network in the host or sandbox. Under MCP 2026-07-28, reject metadata-header/body mismatches before routing or policy relies on them. Isolate private caches by verified authorization context, tenant, resource, and policy version; share only data explicitly approved as public. Authorize explicit task/state handles on every operation; neither a connection nor self-reported metadata establishes identity. Where the gateway is an OAuth client, validate authorization-server issuer responses and protect discovery URLs against SSRF. Record protocol and extension versions and test each enabled extension's boundary, including task access/cancellation and MCP Apps sandbox, CSP, bridge messages, and UI-initiated tool authorization. Test bypass, cross-tenant access, malformed traffic, and required-check outages. Required checks fail closed.\n{\"id\": \"E06.1\", \"check\": \"Every governed tool path uses an enforced boundary suited to its internal HTTP, public third-party, or local stdio deployment; agent-controlled code cannot bypass it or obtain backend credentials.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Inventory HTTP, dynamic, CLI/code-mode, wrapper and local-process paths. 2) Trace effective egress, backend credential custody and process/file/env/network restrictions. 3) Internal private networking/mTLS is one option; public services can use agent-side egress and broker-held credentials. 4) Reject any usable unmediated path; do not require operator control of a public provider's network. Use unknown for enforcement outside this repo.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.2\", \"check\": \"The gateway validates its own incoming token audience, issuer, expiry and scopes, and obtains separately authorized, backend-specific credentials while preserving agent and delegated-subject identity.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Trace client-to-gateway and gateway-to-backend credentials independently. 2) Check trusted issuer, audience, grants, expiry and supported exchange/grant. 3) Reject tokens meant for other resources or unchanged incoming-token forwarding used instead of backend authorization. 4) A scoped delegated-user token is valid when the acting agent is verified separately; a vault alone does not create expiring tokens.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.3\", \"check\": \"Every direct, dynamic, CLI/code-mode and wrapper call receives action/resource/tenant/argument authorization, request/response validation, rate limits and decision logging.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Enumerate every execution path, not only tools/call. 2) Trace the same authorization, validation, quota and logging policy in each. 3) Reject alternate paths that invoke a disabled or denied tool, authorize only a tool name, or change tenant/resource authority. Use unknown for unavailable implementation evidence.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.4\", \"check\": \"If a required check (policy engine, scanner, token check) errors or times out, the call is blocked.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the policy engine, scanner, and token check. 2) Check each error blocks the call. 3) Answer no if any error branch allows the call or logs and continues, or a config flag defaults to fail-open.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.5\", \"check\": \"Under MCP 2026-07-28, relevant header/body mismatches are rejected before routing or policy relies on them, and private caches/state/task handles are isolated by verified authorization context, tenant, resource and policy version.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Identify supported protocol versions. 2) For 2026-07-28, trace version/method/name/parameter header validation before affected routing/policy decisions. 3) Trace cache keys/invalidation and every task/state-handle operation, including status/results and cancellation where present. 4) Reject cross-tenant/caller reads or stale grants after revocation; permit shared cache entries only when explicitly public. 5) Do not require removed protocol sessions for 2026-07-28; test legacy session binding only when that version is enabled.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.6\", \"check\": \"If the gateway is itself an OAuth client, it checks the authorization server's issuer (iss, RFC 9207) and blocks private and metadata addresses in discovery URLs. Answer yes with the code line, or yes citing the config that shows it isn't an OAuth client.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Check whether the gateway acts as an OAuth client (gets tokens, follows discovery or metadata URLs). 2) If so, check RFC 9207 issuer-response comparison and rejection when an advertised required iss is missing; do not require an absent iss when the selected protocol permits it. Check it blocks unauthorized private, loopback, and metadata destinations, including on redirects and DNS resolution. Explicitly approved internal issuer endpoints may be allowed by trusted configuration; untrusted discovery must not widen that allowlist. 3) Answer no if either is missing. If it is not an OAuth client, answer yes citing the config that shows that.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.7\", \"check\": \"Enabled MCP extensions have recorded versions and enforced boundaries, including Tasks ownership/cancellation and Apps sandbox/CSP/bridge/tool-call authorization where present.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Inventory enabled extensions and versions from client/server/host configuration. 2) Trace extension-specific authorization, task ownership/status/results/cancellation, and Apps host sandbox, CSP, bridge-message validation and UI-triggered tool policy. 3) Reject a bypass or missing required boundary. 4) Answer yes for absent extensions only with configuration evidence; answer unknown for external host behavior not visible here.\"}\n===== E07 Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message, even validly signed ones. Validate message types and schemas, and check what that peer is allowed to ask for. Where a replay could repeat an action, check freshness and track nonces or request IDs. Checking the sender alone doesn't stop replays. Test faked identity, replayed requests, requests across tenants, and instructions passed along by a compromised peer. Verify signed agent cards where they exist. A card says who an agent is, not what it may do. Check callback and webhook URLs against SSRF. A valid sender doesn't make a message's content trusted.\n{\"id\": \"E07.1\", \"check\": \"Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is authenticated to a specific sending agent (mTLS identity, verified token subject). 3) Answer no if any route accepts unauthenticated messages, trusts a self-declared sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E07.2\", \"check\": \"Message types and schemas are validated, and each request is checked against what that peer is allowed to ask for, including tenant.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open the peer message handler. 2) Check message type and schema validation. 3) Check a per-peer allowlist of request types and tenants, keyed on the authenticated sender. 4) Answer no if schemas are unchecked, any authenticated peer can ask for anything, or tenant is taken from the message body.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E07.3\", \"check\": \"Action requests carry a nonce or request ID and a freshness check, and replays are rejected or do not repeat side effects.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find action request handling. 2) Check for a nonce or request ID plus a freshness (timestamp) check, with seen IDs stored. 3) Answer no if no replay check exists, the nonce is never stored or compared, or a repeated ID repeats side effects.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E07.4\", \"check\": \"Peer message content is handled as untrusted data and is not placed into system or instruction prompts.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Trace peer message content to the prompt builder. 2) Check it goes into user or tool-result content as untrusted data. 3) Answer no if any path places it into the system prompt or an instruction template.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E07.5\", \"check\": \"Callback and webhook URLs are checked against SSRF, with private and metadata addresses blocked.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find code that calls callback or webhook URLs from peers. 2) Check URL validation blocks private, loopback, link-local, and metadata addresses (169.254.169.254). 3) Answer no if any callback is fetched without the check, or only the hostname text is checked and not the resolved address.\"}\n===== E08 Give sub-agents only the powers approved for their task. Preserve the verified original subject and current actor through each handoff and enforce their task, tenant, resource, and audience limits where the action runs. Use supported token exchange or narrow task credentials rather than copying a parent's full credential. A parent must not gain a denied power by asking a more powerful peer to act without separate valid approval. For RFC 8693 tokens, earlier nested actors are provenance only and never add access. An actor chain or signed identity does not prove that a requested action was approved. Test legitimate delegation and that escalation attempt.\n{\"id\": \"E08.1\", \"check\": \"Each child gets a credential narrowed to its approved task (for example by token exchange or transaction tokens), never the parent's full credential.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where a child agent gets its credential. 2) Check it is a narrowed token for the task (token exchange, transaction token, scoped-down role). 3) Answer no if any spawn path passes the parent's token, API key, or full role, or the child inherits the parent's environment credentials.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E08.2\", \"check\": \"Authorization at the action uses the original subject and the current actor, and earlier actors in the delegation chain never add access.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open authorization code for delegated actions. 2) Check it decides on the original subject and the current actor. 3) Answer no if it grants access because of any earlier actor in the chain (nested `act` claims, parent identity) or a union of chain permissions.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E08.3\", \"check\": \"An action the parent was denied is also denied when routed through a more powerful peer, unless it carries its own explicit approval.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find how a parent asks a peer or child to act. 2) Check the request carries the parent's limits and the peer re-checks them, or requires its own explicit approval. 3) Answer no if a peer acts with its own wider permissions on a parent's request without that check.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E08.4\", \"check\": \"Downstream services reject the parent's token when the child presents it (audience-bound tokens).\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find how child tokens are issued and how downstream services validate tokens. 2) Check tokens are audience-bound and services verify `aud`. 3) Answer no if audience is unset, a wildcard, or not checked. Answer unknown if downstream services are outside this repo.\"}\n===== E09 Run a drill across a parent, nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks, where they exist. Check that the stop reaches every descendant within the set time. It must revoke access as needed and prevent orphaned retries or restarts. Record how outside effects that already happened are reconciled.\n{\"id\": \"E09.1\", \"check\": \"A stop signal from the root reaches every descendant: nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the stop handler. 2) Check it reaches nested children, remote workers, queued jobs, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks (cancel calls, MCP `notifications/cancelled`). 3) Answer no if any of these that exists in the code is not reached, or stop only sets an in-process flag that remote workers never read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E09.2\", \"check\": \"Stopping revokes descendants' credentials or leases, and leases or tokens are short-lived, so a disconnected worker loses authority within the stop time limit.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open the stop path and credential issuing code. 2) Check stopping revokes descendants' tokens or leases. 3) Check token or lease lifetime fits within the stop time limit. 4) Answer no if no revocation exists, or tokens are long-lived so a disconnected worker keeps authority.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E09.3\", \"check\": \"Queues and schedulers refuse new work, retries, and restarts for a stopped tree.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find queue consumers, schedulers, and retry logic. 2) Check each looks up the stopped state before running new work, retries, or restarts. 3) Answer no if any consumer, retry decorator, or restart policy runs without that check.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E09.4\", \"check\": \"Outside effects already completed are recorded for reconciliation.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open the stop path. 2) Check it records outside effects already completed (tool calls, writes, sent messages) for reconciliation. 3) Answer no if nothing is recorded, or only in-flight work is listed.\"}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Tools are keyed by verified server identity (endpoint, credential, or registry namespace) plus tool name, never by bare tool name or a server's self-reported name.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the tool registry or lookup map. 2) Check its key is a verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace plus tool name. 3) Answer no if tools are keyed by bare tool name or the server's self-reported name (`serverInfo.name`), or a later server overwrites an earlier entry with the same tool name.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.2\",\n  \"check\": \"The registry flags duplicate and lookalike tool names across servers.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"attempt_categories\": [\n    \"repeated_confusables\",\n    \"multiple_edits\",\n    \"normalization_boundary\"\n  ],\n  \"verify\": \"1) Trace name comparison across servers. 2) Construct repeated confusable substitutions, multiple edits and normalization-boundary examples, starting from an existing tool name; record canonical outputs, comparison result and registration outcome. 3) Answer no if a duplicate or demonstrated lookalike is accepted without a conflict flag. The existence of normalization/edit-distance code is insufficient; namespacing and approval binding do not satisfy this separate check.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Approval is bound to the verified server identity, so a new server with a matching tool name or self-reported name does not inherit approval or replace the approved tool.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where tool approval is stored and checked. 2) Check approval is keyed by verified server identity, not tool name or self-reported server name. 3) Answer no if a new server with a matching tool name or server name would count as approved or replace the approved tool.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-499x1leg/skill/scripts/review_coverage.py\", line 184, in <module>\n    main()\n    ~~~~^^\n  File \"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-499x1leg/skill/scripts/review_coverage.py\", line 160, in main\n    meta = next(c for c in table[args.check.split('.')[0]]['checks'] if c['id'] == args.check)\nStopIteration","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c4b6767-3afe-4fbc-ad1e-9f5c27d75379","uuid":"bf99befc-f77d-48c5-bad3-25de5e71cb19","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:50:30.359Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"===== E05 Identify each tool by a verified server identity plus the tool name. Base server identity on the verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace. A server's self-reported name is neither unique nor trustworthy. Flag lookalike and duplicate names across servers. Test that a new server can't quietly swap its tool in for an approved one.\n{\"id\": \"E05.1\", \"check\": \"Tools are keyed by verified server identity (endpoint, credential, or registry namespace) plus tool name, never by bare tool name or a server's self-reported name.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the tool registry or lookup map. 2) Check its key is a verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace plus tool name. 3) Answer no if tools are keyed by bare tool name or the server's self-reported name (`serverInfo.name`), or a later server overwrites an earlier entry with the same tool name.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E05.2\", \"check\": \"The registry flags duplicate and lookalike tool names across servers.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"attempt_categories\": [\"repeated_confusables\", \"multiple_edits\", \"normalization_boundary\"], \"verify\": \"1) Trace name comparison across servers. 2) Construct repeated confusable substitutions, multiple edits and normalization-boundary examples, starting from an existing tool name; record canonical outputs, comparison result and registration outcome. 3) Answer no if a duplicate or demonstrated lookalike is accepted without a conflict flag. The existence of normalization/edit-distance code is insufficient; namespacing and approval binding do not satisfy this separate check.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E05.3\", \"check\": \"Approval is bound to the verified server identity, so a new server with a matching tool name or self-reported name does not inherit approval or replace the approved tool.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where tool approval is stored and checked. 2) Check approval is keyed by verified server identity, not tool name or self-reported server name. 3) Answer no if a new server with a matching tool name or server name would count as approved or replace the approved tool.\"}\n===== E06 Send MCP calls through a gateway or equivalent enforcement layer the agent cannot bypass. Choose controls for internal HTTP servers, public third-party services, and local stdio servers; private networking and mTLS are one internal deployment pattern, not universal MCP requirements. Authenticate each caller, preserve agent and delegated-subject identity, and authorize each action's tool, operation, resource, tenant, and arguments. Apply the same policy to direct calls, dynamic tools, CLI/code mode, and wrappers. Validate calls and responses, enforce rate limits, and log every decision. For HTTP OAuth, validate access tokens for the gateway's own audience, issuer, expiry, and scopes; obtain separately authorized backend credentials through a trusted issuer or supported exchange. Never accept a token for another resource or relay it unchanged as a substitute for backend authorization. Keep backend secrets and tokens away from agent-controlled execution paths. Restrict local process launch, files, environment, credentials, and network in the host or sandbox. Under MCP 2026-07-28, reject metadata-header/body mismatches before routing or policy relies on them. Isolate private caches by verified authorization context, tenant, resource, and policy version; share only data explicitly approved as public. Authorize explicit task/state handles on every operation; neither a connection nor self-reported metadata establishes identity. Where the gateway is an OAuth client, validate authorization-server issuer responses and protect discovery URLs against SSRF. Record protocol and extension versions and test each enabled extension's boundary, including task access/cancellation and MCP Apps sandbox, CSP, bridge messages, and UI-initiated tool authorization. Test bypass, cross-tenant access, malformed traffic, and required-check outages. Required checks fail closed.\n{\"id\": \"E06.1\", \"check\": \"Every governed tool path uses an enforced boundary suited to its internal HTTP, public third-party, or local stdio deployment; agent-controlled code cannot bypass it or obtain backend credentials.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Inventory HTTP, dynamic, CLI/code-mode, wrapper and local-process paths. 2) Trace effective egress, backend credential custody and process/file/env/network restrictions. 3) Internal private networking/mTLS is one option; public services can use agent-side egress and broker-held credentials. 4) Reject any usable unmediated path; do not require operator control of a public provider's network. Use unknown for enforcement outside this repo.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.2\", \"check\": \"The gateway validates its own incoming token audience, issuer, expiry and scopes, and obtains separately authorized, backend-specific credentials while preserving agent and delegated-subject identity.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Trace client-to-gateway and gateway-to-backend credentials independently. 2) Check trusted issuer, audience, grants, expiry and supported exchange/grant. 3) Reject tokens meant for other resources or unchanged incoming-token forwarding used instead of backend authorization. 4) A scoped delegated-user token is valid when the acting agent is verified separately; a vault alone does not create expiring tokens.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.3\", \"check\": \"Every direct, dynamic, CLI/code-mode and wrapper call receives action/resource/tenant/argument authorization, request/response validation, rate limits and decision logging.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Enumerate every execution path, not only tools/call. 2) Trace the same authorization, validation, quota and logging policy in each. 3) Reject alternate paths that invoke a disabled or denied tool, authorize only a tool name, or change tenant/resource authority. Use unknown for unavailable implementation evidence.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.4\", \"check\": \"If a required check (policy engine, scanner, token check) errors or times out, the call is blocked.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the policy engine, scanner, and token check. 2) Check each error blocks the call. 3) Answer no if any error branch allows the call or logs and continues, or a config flag defaults to fail-open.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.5\", \"check\": \"Under MCP 2026-07-28, relevant header/body mismatches are rejected before routing or policy relies on them, and private caches/state/task handles are isolated by verified authorization context, tenant, resource and policy version.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Identify supported protocol versions. 2) For 2026-07-28, trace version/method/name/parameter header validation before affected routing/policy decisions. 3) Trace cache keys/invalidation and every task/state-handle operation, including status/results and cancellation where present. 4) Reject cross-tenant/caller reads or stale grants after revocation; permit shared cache entries only when explicitly public. 5) Do not require removed protocol sessions for 2026-07-28; test legacy session binding only when that version is enabled.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.6\", \"check\": \"If the gateway is itself an OAuth client, it checks the authorization server's issuer (iss, RFC 9207) and blocks private and metadata addresses in discovery URLs. Answer yes with the code line, or yes citing the config that shows it isn't an OAuth client.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Check whether the gateway acts as an OAuth client (gets tokens, follows discovery or metadata URLs). 2) If so, check RFC 9207 issuer-response comparison and rejection when an advertised required iss is missing; do not require an absent iss when the selected protocol permits it. Check it blocks unauthorized private, loopback, and metadata destinations, including on redirects and DNS resolution. Explicitly approved internal issuer endpoints may be allowed by trusted configuration; untrusted discovery must not widen that allowlist. 3) Answer no if either is missing. If it is not an OAuth client, answer yes citing the config that shows that.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E06.7\", \"check\": \"Enabled MCP extensions have recorded versions and enforced boundaries, including Tasks ownership/cancellation and Apps sandbox/CSP/bridge/tool-call authorization where present.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Inventory enabled extensions and versions from client/server/host configuration. 2) Trace extension-specific authorization, task ownership/status/results/cancellation, and Apps host sandbox, CSP, bridge-message validation and UI-triggered tool policy. 3) Reject a bypass or missing required boundary. 4) Answer yes for absent extensions only with configuration evidence; answer unknown for external host behavior not visible here.\"}\n===== E07 Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message, even validly signed ones. Validate message types and schemas, and check what that peer is allowed to ask for. Where a replay could repeat an action, check freshness and track nonces or request IDs. Checking the sender alone doesn't stop replays. Test faked identity, replayed requests, requests across tenants, and instructions passed along by a compromised peer. Verify signed agent cards where they exist. A card says who an agent is, not what it may do. Check callback and webhook URLs against SSRF. A valid sender doesn't make a message's content trusted.\n{\"id\": \"E07.1\", \"check\": \"Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is authenticated to a specific sending agent (mTLS identity, verified token subject). 3) Answer no if any route accepts unauthenticated messages, trusts a self-declared sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E07.2\", \"check\": \"Message types and schemas are validated, and each request is checked against what that peer is allowed to ask for, including tenant.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open the peer message handler. 2) Check message type and schema validation. 3) Check a per-peer allowlist of request types and tenants, keyed on the authenticated sender. 4) Answer no if schemas are unchecked, any authenticated peer can ask for anything, or tenant is taken from the message body.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E07.3\", \"check\": \"Action requests carry a nonce or request ID and a freshness check, and replays are rejected or do not repeat side effects.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find action request handling. 2) Check for a nonce or request ID plus a freshness (timestamp) check, with seen IDs stored. 3) Answer no if no replay check exists, the nonce is never stored or compared, or a repeated ID repeats side effects.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E07.4\", \"check\": \"Peer message content is handled as untrusted data and is not placed into system or instruction prompts.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Trace peer message content to the prompt builder. 2) Check it goes into user or tool-result content as untrusted data. 3) Answer no if any path places it into the system prompt or an instruction template.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E07.5\", \"check\": \"Callback and webhook URLs are checked against SSRF, with private and metadata addresses blocked.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find code that calls callback or webhook URLs from peers. 2) Check URL validation blocks private, loopback, link-local, and metadata addresses (169.254.169.254). 3) Answer no if any callback is fetched without the check, or only the hostname text is checked and not the resolved address.\"}\n===== E08 Give sub-agents only the powers approved for their task. Preserve the verified original subject and current actor through each handoff and enforce their task, tenant, resource, and audience limits where the action runs. Use supported token exchange or narrow task credentials rather than copying a parent's full credential. A parent must not gain a denied power by asking a more powerful peer to act without separate valid approval. For RFC 8693 tokens, earlier nested actors are provenance only and never add access. An actor chain or signed identity does not prove that a requested action was approved. Test legitimate delegation and that escalation attempt.\n{\"id\": \"E08.1\", \"check\": \"Each child gets a credential narrowed to its approved task (for example by token exchange or transaction tokens), never the parent's full credential.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where a child agent gets its credential. 2) Check it is a narrowed token for the task (token exchange, transaction token, scoped-down role). 3) Answer no if any spawn path passes the parent's token, API key, or full role, or the child inherits the parent's environment credentials.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E08.2\", \"check\": \"Authorization at the action uses the original subject and the current actor, and earlier actors in the delegation chain never add access.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open authorization code for delegated actions. 2) Check it decides on the original subject and the current actor. 3) Answer no if it grants access because of any earlier actor in the chain (nested `act` claims, parent identity) or a union of chain permissions.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E08.3\", \"check\": \"An action the parent was denied is also denied when routed through a more powerful peer, unless it carries its own explicit approval.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find how a parent asks a peer or child to act. 2) Check the request carries the parent's limits and the peer re-checks them, or requires its own explicit approval. 3) Answer no if a peer acts with its own wider permissions on a parent's request without that check.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E08.4\", \"check\": \"Downstream services reject the parent's token when the child presents it (audience-bound tokens).\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find how child tokens are issued and how downstream services validate tokens. 2) Check tokens are audience-bound and services verify `aud`. 3) Answer no if audience is unset, a wildcard, or not checked. Answer unknown if downstream services are outside this repo.\"}\n===== E09 Run a drill across a parent, nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks, where they exist. Check that the stop reaches every descendant within the set time. It must revoke access as needed and prevent orphaned retries or restarts. Record how outside effects that already happened are reconciled.\n{\"id\": \"E09.1\", \"check\": \"A stop signal from the root reaches every descendant: nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the stop handler. 2) Check it reaches nested children, remote workers, queued jobs, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks (cancel calls, MCP `notifications/cancelled`). 3) Answer no if any of these that exists in the code is not reached, or stop only sets an in-process flag that remote workers never read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E09.2\", \"check\": \"Stopping revokes descendants' credentials or leases, and leases or tokens are short-lived, so a disconnected worker loses authority within the stop time limit.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open the stop path and credential issuing code. 2) Check stopping revokes descendants' tokens or leases. 3) Check token or lease lifetime fits within the stop time limit. 4) Answer no if no revocation exists, or tokens are long-lived so a disconnected worker keeps authority.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E09.3\", \"check\": \"Queues and schedulers refuse new work, retries, and restarts for a stopped tree.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find queue consumers, schedulers, and retry logic. 2) Check each looks up the stopped state before running new work, retries, or restarts. 3) Answer no if any consumer, retry decorator, or restart policy runs without that check.\"}\n{\"id\": \"E09.4\", \"check\": \"Outside effects already completed are recorded for reconciliation.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Open the stop path. 2) Check it records outside effects already completed (tool calls, writes, sent messages) for reconciliation. 3) Answer no if nothing is recorded, or only in-flight work is listed.\"}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Tools are keyed by verified server identity (endpoint, credential, or registry namespace) plus tool name, never by bare tool name or a server's self-reported name.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the tool registry or lookup map. 2) Check its key is a verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace plus tool name. 3) Answer no if tools are keyed by bare tool name or the server's self-reported name (`serverInfo.name`), or a later server overwrites an earlier entry with the same tool name.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.2\",\n  \"check\": \"The registry flags duplicate and lookalike tool names across servers.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"attempt_categories\": [\n    \"repeated_confusables\",\n    \"multiple_edits\",\n    \"normalization_boundary\"\n  ],\n  \"verify\": \"1) Trace name comparison across servers. 2) Construct repeated confusable substitutions, multiple edits and normalization-boundary examples, starting from an existing tool name; record canonical outputs, comparison result and registration outcome. 3) Answer no if a duplicate or demonstrated lookalike is accepted without a conflict flag. The existence of normalization/edit-distance code is insufficient; namespacing and approval binding do not satisfy this separate check.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Approval is bound to the verified server identity, so a new server with a matching tool name or self-reported name does not inherit approval or replace the approved tool.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where tool approval is stored and checked. 2) Check approval is keyed by verified server identity, not tool name or self-reported server name. 3) Answer no if a new server with a matching tool name or server name would count as approved or replace the approved tool.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-499x1leg/skill/scripts/review_coverage.py\", line 184, in <module>\n    main()\n    ~~~~^^\n  File \"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-499x1leg/skill/scripts/review_coverage.py\", line 160, in main\n    meta = next(c for c in table[args.check.split('.')[0]]['checks'] if c['id'] == args.check)\nStopIteration","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FBUmx23nbwfVwekTGTqEe8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDWzsyDE75eYdEX3VDvy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LGJ8WaEJmv9g64arP6rvHP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-499x1leg/agent && cat -n src/tools/executor.ts src/agent/loop.ts release/manifest.json src/config.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15271,"cache_read_input_tokens":26358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15271},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c4b6767-3afe-4fbc-ad1e-9f5c27d75379","uuid":"9e9c6023-0c11-42be-a7cd-f0f5b92b3557","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:50:30.811Z","request_id":"req_011CgDWzsgrCBpuEnCBvRVxs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LGJ8WaEJmv9g64arP6rvHP":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-499x1leg/agent && cat -n src/tools/executor.ts src/agent/loop.ts release/manifest.json src/config.ts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LGJ8WaEJmv9g64arP6rvHP","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\timport type Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\n     2\timport { allowlist, policy } from \"../config.js\";\n     3\timport { audit, AuditUnavailable, redactPhi } from \"../audit/recorder.js\";\n     4\timport { BudgetExceeded, type RunBudget } from \"../agent/budget.js\";\n     5\timport type { ContextSize } from \"../agent/context-size.js\";\n     6\timport { AGENT_INSTANCE_ID, type RunContext } from \"../agent/identity.js\";\n     7\timport { Halted, killSwitch } from \"../control/kill-switch.js\";\n     8\timport type { Ehr } from \"../integrations/ehr-mcp.js\";\n     9\timport { payments } from \"../integrations/payments.js\";\n    10\timport { render, sms, TEMPLATES, type TemplateId } from \"../integrations/sms.js\";\n    11\timport { checkEligibilityForAppointment } from \"../workflows/eligibility-check.js\";\n    12\timport { checkApproval, requestApproval } from \"./approvals.js\";\n    13\timport type { RegisteredTool, ToolRegistry } from \"./registry.js\";\n    14\t\n    15\texport interface Decision {\n    16\t  contextSize: ContextSize;\n    17\t  budget: RunBudget;\n    18\t}\n    19\t\n    20\tconst ALLOWED = new Set(allowlist.tools.map((t) => t.tool));\n    21\t// Arguments the harness consumes itself; they are never forwarded to a tool.\n    22\tconst CONTROL_ARGS = new Set([\"approvalId\", \"clinicId\"]);\n    23\t\n    24\tfunction toolResult(id: string, content: unknown, isError = false): Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam {\n    25\t  return { type: \"tool_result\", tool_use_id: id, content: JSON.stringify(content), is_error: isError };\n    26\t}\n    27\t\n    28\tfunction summarize(tool: string, args: Record<string, unknown>): string {\n    29\t  return `${tool}(${Object.entries(args)\n    30\t    .map(([k, v]) => `${k}=${JSON.stringify(v)}`)\n    31\t    .join(\", \")})`.slice(0, 500);\n    32\t}\n    33\t\n    34\texport async function executeTool(\n    35\t  registry: ToolRegistry,\n    36\t  ctx: RunContext,\n    37\t  call: Anthropic.ToolUseBlock,\n    38\t  d: Decision,\n    39\t): Promise<Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam> {\n    40\t  const input = (call.input ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>;\n    41\t  const base = {\n    42\t    ...ctx.identity(),\n    43\t    runId: ctx.runId,\n    44\t    subject: ctx.subject,\n    45\t    tool: call.name,\n    46\t    toolUseId: call.id,\n    47\t    policyVersion: policy.version,\n    48\t    context: d.contextSize,\n    49\t  };\n    50\t  const deny = async (reason: string) => {\n    51\t    await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.denied\", reason });\n    52\t    return toolResult(call.id, { error: \"denied\", reason }, true);\n    53\t  };\n    54\t\n    55\t  if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\"not_allowlisted\");\n    56\t  const tool = registry.get(call.name);\n    57\t  if (!tool) return deny(\"not_registered\");\n    58\t\n    59\t  await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n    60\t  await d.budget.toolCall(call.name);\n    61\t\n    62\t  // Front-desk staff working one clinic's chat can act for a sibling clinic in the group.\n    63\t  const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;\n    64\t  const args = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(input).filter(([k]) => !CONTROL_ARGS.has(k)));\n    65\t\n    66\t  let approvalId: string | undefined;\n    67\t  if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {\n    68\t    if (typeof input.approvalId !== \"string\") {\n    69\t      const rec = await requestApproval({\n    70\t        tool: call.name,\n    71\t        tenantId: clinicId,\n    72\t        agentInstanceId: AGENT_INSTANCE_ID,\n    73\t        runId: ctx.runId,\n    74\t        args,\n    75\t        summary: summarize(call.name, args),\n    76\t      });\n    77\t      await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.approval_requested\", approvalId: rec.id });\n    78\t      return toolResult(call.id, { status: \"pending_approval\", approvalId: rec.id, expiresAt: rec.expiresAt });\n    79\t    }\n    80\t    const check = await checkApproval({ approvalId: input.approvalId, tool: call.name, tenantId: clinicId, args });\n    81\t    if (!check.ok) return deny(check.reason);\n    82\t    approvalId = check.approval.id;\n    83\t  }\n    84\t\n    85\t  try {\n    86\t    const raw = await tool.invoke(args, { clinicId, signal: d.budget.signal, runCtx: ctx, context: d.contextSize });\n    87\t    ctx.log.info({ tool: call.name, toolUseId: call.id, clinicId, result: raw }, \"tool result\");\n    88\t    const safe = redactPhi(raw);\n    89\t    await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });\n    90\t    return toolResult(call.id, safe);\n    91\t  } catch (err) {\n    92\t    if (err instanceof Halted || err instanceof BudgetExceeded || err instanceof AuditUnavailable) throw err;\n    93\t    await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.failed\", approvalId, reason: (err as Error).message.slice(0, 300) });\n    94\t    return toolResult(call.id, { error: \"tool_failed\" }, true);\n    95\t  }\n    96\t}\n    97\t\n    98\ttype Native = Omit<RegisteredTool, \"key\" | \"serverId\">;\n    99\t\n   100\texport function nativeTools(ehr: Ehr): Record<string, Native[]> {\n   101\t  const contact = async (clinicId: string, patientId: string, signal: AbortSignal) =>\n   102\t    (await ehr.call(\"get_patient_contact\", { patientId }, { clinicId, signal })) as { phone: string; smsOptIn: boolean; firstName: string };\n   103\t\n   104\t  return {\n   105\t    payments: [\n   106\t      {\n   107\t        name: \"refund_deposit\",\n   108\t        definition: {\n   109\t          name: \"payments__refund_deposit\",\n   110\t          description: \"Refund a patient's appointment deposit. Requires staff approval.\",\n   111\t          input_schema: {\n   112\t            type: \"object\",\n   113\t            properties: {\n   114\t              depositId: { type: \"string\" },\n   115\t              reason: { type: \"string\", enum: [\"no_show_waived\", \"clinic_cancelled\", \"billing_error\"] },\n   116\t              approvalId: { type: \"string\" },\n   117\t            },\n   118\t            required: [\"depositId\", \"reason\"],\n   119\t          },\n   120\t        },\n   121\t        invoke: async (a, o) =>\n   122\t          payments.refundDeposit(o.clinicId, { depositId: String(a.depositId), reason: String(a.reason), idempotencyKey: `refund-${a.depositId}` }, o.signal),\n   123\t      },\n   124\t    ],\n   125\t    sms: [\n   126\t      {\n   127\t        name: \"send_to_patient\",\n   128\t        definition: {\n   129\t          name: \"sms__send_to_patient\",\n   130\t          description: \"Send a templated SMS to the phone number on the patient's record.\",\n   131\t          input_schema: {\n   132\t            type: \"object\",\n   133\t            properties: {\n   134\t              patientId: { type: \"string\" },\n   135\t              template: { type: \"string\", enum: Object.keys(TEMPLATES) },\n   136\t              vars: { type: \"object\", additionalProperties: { type: \"string\" } },\n   137\t            },\n   138\t            required: [\"patientId\", \"template\"],\n   139\t          },\n   140\t        },\n   141\t        invoke: async (a, o) => {\n   142\t          const c = await contact(o.clinicId, String(a.patientId), o.signal);\n   143\t          if (!c.smsOptIn) throw new Error(\"patient has not opted in to SMS\");\n   144\t          const body = render(a.template as TemplateId, { firstName: c.firstName, ...((a.vars as Record<string, string>) ?? {}) });\n   145\t          return sms.send(o.clinicId, c.phone, body, o.signal);\n   146\t        },\n   147\t      },\n   148\t      {\n   149\t        name: \"send_freeform\",\n   150\t        definition: {\n   151\t          name: \"sms__send_freeform\",\n   152\t          description: \"Send a non-template SMS to the patient's phone on record. Requires staff approval.\",\n   153\t          input_schema: {\n   154\t            type: \"object\",\n   155\t            properties: { patientId: { type: \"string\" }, body: { type: \"string\", maxLength: 320 }, approvalId: { type: \"string\" } },\n   156\t            required: [\"patientId\", \"body\"],\n   157\t          },\n   158\t        },\n   159\t        invoke: async (a, o) => {\n   160\t          const c = await contact(o.clinicId, String(a.patientId), o.signal);\n   161\t          if (!c.smsOptIn) throw new Error(\"patient has not opted in to SMS\");\n   162\t          return sms.send(o.clinicId, c.phone, String(a.body).slice(0, 320), o.signal);\n   163\t        },\n   164\t      },\n   165\t    ],\n   166\t    insurance: [\n   167\t      {\n   168\t        name: \"check_eligibility\",\n   169\t        definition: {\n   170\t          name: \"insurance__check_eligibility\",\n   171\t          description: \"Check whether the patient's insurance covers an appointment.\",\n   172\t          input_schema: { type: \"object\", properties: { appointmentId: { type: \"string\" } }, required: [\"appointmentId\"] },\n   173\t        },\n   174\t        invoke: async (a, o) =>\n   175\t          checkEligibilityForAppointment(ehr, { appointmentId: String(a.appointmentId) }, {\n   176\t            clinicId: o.clinicId,\n   177\t            ctx: o.runCtx as RunContext,\n   178\t            signal: o.signal,\n   179\t            context: o.context,\n   180\t          }),\n   181\t      },\n   182\t    ],\n   183\t  };\n   184\t}\n     1\timport Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\n     2\timport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n     3\timport { join } from \"node:path\";\n     4\timport { AGENT_MODEL, budgets, ROOT } from \"../config.js\";\n     5\timport { audit, AuditUnavailable } from \"../audit/recorder.js\";\n     6\timport { Halted, killSwitch } from \"../control/kill-switch.js\";\n     7\timport { executeTool } from \"../tools/executor.js\";\n     8\timport type { ToolRegistry } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\n     9\timport { BudgetExceeded, DynamoQuotaStore, RunBudget } from \"./budget.js\";\n    10\timport { classifyIntent } from \"./classifier.js\";\n    11\timport { completeFromUsage, measureBeforeCall, spanAttributes } from \"./context-size.js\";\n    12\timport type { RunContext } from \"./identity.js\";\n    13\t\n    14\tconst SYSTEM_TEMPLATE = readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"prompts/system.md\"), \"utf8\");\n    15\tconst anthropic = new Anthropic({ maxRetries: 1 });\n    16\tconst quotaStore = new DynamoQuotaStore();\n    17\t\n    18\texport interface AgentReply {\n    19\t  text: string;\n    20\t  handoff: null | { reason: string };\n    21\t}\n    22\t\n    23\tfunction escapeTags(s: string): string {\n    24\t  return s.replace(/</g, \"&lt;\").replace(/>/g, \"&gt;\");\n    25\t}\n    26\t\n    27\texport async function runAgent(\n    28\t  registry: ToolRegistry,\n    29\t  ctx: RunContext,\n    30\t  clinic: { name: string },\n    31\t  patientText: string,\n    32\t): Promise<AgentReply> {\n    33\t  const ident = () => ({ ...ctx.identity(), runId: ctx.runId, subject: ctx.subject });\n    34\t  const budget = new RunBudget(budgets, quotaStore, { tenantId: ctx.tenantId, subjectId: ctx.subject.id });\n    35\t  const unregister = killSwitch.register(ctx.runId, ctx.tenantId, budget.abort);\n    36\t  await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.started\", detail: { channel: ctx.channel } });\n    37\t\n    38\t  try {\n    39\t    await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n    40\t\n    41\t    const intent = await classifyIntent(anthropic, patientText);\n    42\t    await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"intent.classified\", detail: { ...intent } });\n    43\t    if (intent.failure) ctx.log.warn({ classifier: intent.requestedModel, failure: intent.failure }, \"intent classifier control failure\");\n    44\t    if (intent.route === \"staff\") {\n    45\t      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason: `routed_to_staff:${intent.failure ?? intent.intent}` });\n    46\t      return { text: \"Thanks. A member of our front desk team will get back to you shortly.\", handoff: { reason: intent.failure ?? String(intent.intent) } };\n    47\t    }\n    48\t\n    49\t    const system = SYSTEM_TEMPLATE.replace(\"{{clinicName}}\", clinic.name);\n    50\t    const tools = registry.definitions();\n    51\t    const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\n    52\t      { role: \"user\", content: `<patient_message>${escapeTags(patientText)}</patient_message>` },\n    53\t    ];\n    54\t\n    55\t    for (;;) {\n    56\t      budget.turn();\n    57\t      await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n    58\t\n    59\t      const req = { model: AGENT_MODEL, system, tools, messages };\n    60\t      const pre = await measureBeforeCall(anthropic, req, budget.signal);\n    61\t      const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\n    62\t      const contextSize = completeFromUsage(pre, res.usage);\n    63\t      await budget.recordUsage(res.usage, AGENT_MODEL);\n    64\t\n    65\t      const toolUses = res.content.filter((b): b is Anthropic.ToolUseBlock => b.type === \"tool_use\");\n    66\t      await audit.record({\n    67\t        ...ident(),\n    68\t        event: \"model.decision\",\n    69\t        context: contextSize,\n    70\t        detail: {\n    71\t          servedModel: res.model,\n    72\t          stopReason: res.stop_reason,\n    73\t          proposed: toolUses.map((t) => ({ id: t.id, name: t.name })),\n    74\t          span: spanAttributes(contextSize),\n    75\t        },\n    76\t      });\n    77\t\n    78\t      if (res.stop_reason !== \"tool_use\" || toolUses.length === 0) {\n    79\t        const text = res.content\n    80\t          .filter((b): b is Anthropic.TextBlock => b.type === \"text\")\n    81\t          .map((b) => b.text)\n    82\t          .join(\"\\n\")\n    83\t          .slice(0, 320);\n    84\t        await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.completed\" });\n    85\t        return { text, handoff: null };\n    86\t      }\n    87\t\n    88\t      messages.push({ role: \"assistant\", content: res.content });\n    89\t      const results: Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam[] = [];\n    90\t      for (const call of toolUses) {\n    91\t        results.push(await executeTool(registry, ctx, call, { contextSize, budget }));\n    92\t      }\n    93\t      messages.push({ role: \"user\", content: results });\n    94\t    }\n    95\t  } catch (err) {\n    96\t    const reason =\n    97\t      err instanceof BudgetExceeded\n    98\t        ? `budget:${err.limit}`\n    99\t        : err instanceof Halted\n   100\t          ? `halted:${err.scope}`\n   101\t          : err instanceof AuditUnavailable\n   102\t            ? \"audit_unavailable\"\n   103\t            : budget.signal.aborted\n   104\t              ? `aborted:${String((budget.signal.reason as Error)?.message ?? \"\")}`\n   105\t              : `error:${(err as Error).message.slice(0, 200)}`;\n   106\t    try {\n   107\t      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason });\n   108\t    } catch {\n   109\t      ctx.log.error({ runId: ctx.runId, reason }, \"run stopped and audit delivery failed\");\n   110\t    }\n   111\t    return { text: \"Sorry, we couldn't finish that here. Our front desk will follow up.\", handoff: { reason } };\n   112\t  } finally {\n   113\t    budget.dispose();\n   114\t    unregister();\n   115\t  }\n   116\t}\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"release\": \"clinic-agent-3.4.1\",\n     3\t  \"agentTypeId\": \"sha256:7c2e91f04ab35d6e8f1029c4b7a6d3e5f8091a2b3c4d5e6f708192a3b4c5d6e7\",\n     4\t  \"image\": {\n     5\t    \"repository\": \"418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent\",\n     6\t    \"digest\": \"sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\"\n     7\t  },\n     8\t  \"harness\": {\n     9\t    \"version\": \"3.4.1\",\n    10\t    \"gitSha\": \"e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\"\n    11\t  },\n    12\t  \"prompts\": [\n    13\t    { \"path\": \"prompts/system.md\", \"sha256\": \"5d1e0c9b8a7f6e5d4c3b2a1908f7e6d5c4b3a291807f6e5d4c3b2a19087f6e5d\" },\n    14\t    { \"path\": \"prompts/intent-classifier.txt\", \"sha256\": \"a3f9e1d7c5b3a1f9e7d5c3b1a9f7e5d3c1b9a7f5e3d1c9b7a5f3e1d9c7b5a3f1\" }\n    15\t  ],\n    16\t  \"models\": [\n    17\t    {\n    18\t      \"role\": \"agent\",\n    19\t      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n    20\t      \"requestedId\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n    21\t      \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n    22\t      \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n    23\t      \"adapter\": null,\n    24\t      \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n    25\t    },\n    26\t    {\n    27\t      \"role\": \"intent_classifier\",\n    28\t      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n    29\t      \"requestedId\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n    30\t      \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n    31\t      \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n    32\t      \"adapter\": null,\n    33\t      \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n    34\t    }\n    35\t  ],\n    36\t  \"tools\": {\n    37\t    \"allowlist\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\",\n    38\t    \"mcpServers\": [\n    39\t      {\n    40\t        \"id\": \"ehr\",\n    41\t        \"url\": \"https://ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example/mcp\",\n    42\t        \"tlsCertSha256\": \"1f6a9c3e5b7d9f1a3c5e7b9d1f3a5c7e9b1d3f5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c1e3b5d7f9a\",\n    43\t        \"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"\n    44\t      }\n    45\t    ],\n    46\t    \"native\": [\"payments\", \"sms\", \"insurance\"]\n    47\t  },\n    48\t  \"peers\": [\n    49\t    {\n    50\t      \"id\": \"eligibility-agent\",\n    51\t      \"url\": \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example/a2a\",\n    52\t      \"owner\": \"revenue-cycle@northbay-clinics.example\"\n    53\t    }\n    54\t  ],\n    55\t  \"permissions\": {\n    56\t    \"awsRole\": \"arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\",\n    57\t    \"ehrScopes\": [\"patient.read\", \"appointment.read\", \"appointment.write\"],\n    58\t    \"paymentsScopes\": [\"deposits.refund\"],\n    59\t    \"eligibilityScopes\": [\"eligibility:read\"]\n    60\t  },\n    61\t  \"memory\": \"none\",\n    62\t  \"retrieval\": \"none\",\n    63\t  \"network\": { \"policy\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml#clinic-agent-egress\", \"egressProxy\": \"egress-proxy.platform.svc:3128\" },\n    64\t  \"budgets\": \"config/budgets.yaml\",\n    65\t  \"policies\": { \"action\": \"config/policy.yaml\", \"actionPolicyVersion\": \"2026-09-18.3\" }\n    66\t}\n     1\timport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n     2\timport { join } from \"node:path\";\n     3\timport { parse } from \"yaml\";\n     4\t\n     5\texport const ROOT = process.env.CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT ?? process.cwd();\n     6\t\n     7\texport interface Policy {\n     8\t  version: string;\n     9\t  highImpactTools: string[];\n    10\t  approval: { ttlSeconds: number; approverRoles: string[]; table: string };\n    11\t}\n    12\t\n    13\texport interface AllowlistEntry {\n    14\t  tool: string;\n    15\t  reason: string;\n    16\t}\n    17\t\n    18\texport interface Budgets {\n    19\t  run: {\n    20\t    maxTurns: number;\n    21\t    maxWallMs: number;\n    22\t    maxInputTokens: number;\n    23\t    maxOutputTokens: number;\n    24\t    maxCostUsd: number;\n    25\t    maxToolCalls: number;\n    26\t    maxToolCallsPerMinute: number;\n    27\t    maxPeerCalls: number;\n    28\t  };\n    29\t  quotas: {\n    30\t    perSubjectDailyUsd: number;\n    31\t    perTenantDailyUsd: number;\n    32\t    fleetDailyUsd: number;\n    33\t    perTenantToolCallsPerMinute: number;\n    34\t    fleetToolCallsPerMinute: number;\n    35\t  };\n    36\t  pricingUsdPerMTok: Record<string, { input: number; output: number; cacheRead: number; cacheWrite: number }>;\n    37\t  onExceed: \"handoff_to_staff\";\n    38\t}\n    39\t\n    40\tfunction loadYaml<T>(rel: string): T {\n    41\t  return parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, rel), \"utf8\")) as T;\n    42\t}\n    43\t\n    44\texport const policy = loadYaml<Policy>(\"config/policy.yaml\");\n    45\texport const allowlist = loadYaml<{ role: string; tools: AllowlistEntry[] }>(\"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\");\n    46\texport const budgets = loadYaml<Budgets>(\"config/budgets.yaml\");\n    47\texport const manifest = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"release/manifest.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    48\t\n    49\texport const AGENT_MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\";\n    50\texport const CLASSIFIER_MODEL = \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\";\n    51\t\n    52\texport const env = {\n    53\t  region: process.env.AWS_REGION ?? \"us-west-2\",\n    54\t  controlTable: process.env.CONTROL_TABLE ?? \"clinic-agent-control\",\n    55\t  budgetTable: process.env.BUDGET_TABLE ?? \"clinic-agent-budgets\",\n    56\t  auditStream: process.env.AUDIT_STREAM ?? \"clinic-agent-audit\",\n    57\t  smsSigningSecretArn: process.env.SMS_SIGNING_SECRET_ARN ?? \"\",\n    58\t  chatJwksUrl: process.env.CHAT_JWKS_URL ?? \"https://auth.northbay-clinics.example/.well-known/jwks.json\",\n    59\t  chatIssuer: process.env.CHAT_ISSUER ?? \"https://auth.northbay-clinics.example/\",\n    60\t  eligibilityUrl: process.env.ELIGIBILITY_URL ?? \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example/a2a\",\n    61\t  eligibilityIssuer: process.env.ELIGIBILITY_ISSUER ?? \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example\",\n    62\t  tokenExchangeUrl: process.env.TOKEN_EXCHANGE_URL ?? \"https://sts.northbay-clinics.example/oauth2/token\",\n    63\t  accountableParty: \"northbay-clinic-group:patient-access\",\n    64\t  operationalOwner: \"team:agent-platform\",\n    65\t};","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c4b6767-3afe-4fbc-ad1e-9f5c27d75379","uuid":"a9c2733d-d586-4d3c-9a95-6c85d57e65bb","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:50:30.842Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\timport type Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\n     2\timport { allowlist, policy } from \"../config.js\";\n     3\timport { audit, AuditUnavailable, redactPhi } from \"../audit/recorder.js\";\n     4\timport { BudgetExceeded, type RunBudget } from \"../agent/budget.js\";\n     5\timport type { ContextSize } from \"../agent/context-size.js\";\n     6\timport { AGENT_INSTANCE_ID, type RunContext } from \"../agent/identity.js\";\n     7\timport { Halted, killSwitch } from \"../control/kill-switch.js\";\n     8\timport type { Ehr } from \"../integrations/ehr-mcp.js\";\n     9\timport { payments } from \"../integrations/payments.js\";\n    10\timport { render, sms, TEMPLATES, type TemplateId } from \"../integrations/sms.js\";\n    11\timport { checkEligibilityForAppointment } from \"../workflows/eligibility-check.js\";\n    12\timport { checkApproval, requestApproval } from \"./approvals.js\";\n    13\timport type { RegisteredTool, ToolRegistry } from \"./registry.js\";\n    14\t\n    15\texport interface Decision {\n    16\t  contextSize: ContextSize;\n    17\t  budget: RunBudget;\n    18\t}\n    19\t\n    20\tconst ALLOWED = new Set(allowlist.tools.map((t) => t.tool));\n    21\t// Arguments the harness consumes itself; they are never forwarded to a tool.\n    22\tconst CONTROL_ARGS = new Set([\"approvalId\", \"clinicId\"]);\n    23\t\n    24\tfunction toolResult(id: string, content: unknown, isError = false): Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam {\n    25\t  return { type: \"tool_result\", tool_use_id: id, content: JSON.stringify(content), is_error: isError };\n    26\t}\n    27\t\n    28\tfunction summarize(tool: string, args: Record<string, unknown>): string {\n    29\t  return `${tool}(${Object.entries(args)\n    30\t    .map(([k, v]) => `${k}=${JSON.stringify(v)}`)\n    31\t    .join(\", \")})`.slice(0, 500);\n    32\t}\n    33\t\n    34\texport async function executeTool(\n    35\t  registry: ToolRegistry,\n    36\t  ctx: RunContext,\n    37\t  call: Anthropic.ToolUseBlock,\n    38\t  d: Decision,\n    39\t): Promise<Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam> {\n    40\t  const input = (call.input ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>;\n    41\t  const base = {\n    42\t    ...ctx.identity(),\n    43\t    runId: ctx.runId,\n    44\t    subject: ctx.subject,\n    45\t    tool: call.name,\n    46\t    toolUseId: call.id,\n    47\t    policyVersion: policy.version,\n    48\t    context: d.contextSize,\n    49\t  };\n    50\t  const deny = async (reason: string) => {\n    51\t    await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.denied\", reason });\n    52\t    return toolResult(call.id, { error: \"denied\", reason }, true);\n    53\t  };\n    54\t\n    55\t  if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\"not_allowlisted\");\n    56\t  const tool = registry.get(call.name);\n    57\t  if (!tool) return deny(\"not_registered\");\n    58\t\n    59\t  await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n    60\t  await d.budget.toolCall(call.name);\n    61\t\n    62\t  // Front-desk staff working one clinic's chat can act for a sibling clinic in the group.\n    63\t  const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;\n    64\t  const args = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(input).filter(([k]) => !CONTROL_ARGS.has(k)));\n    65\t\n    66\t  let approvalId: string | undefined;\n    67\t  if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {\n    68\t    if (typeof input.approvalId !== \"string\") {\n    69\t      const rec = await requestApproval({\n    70\t        tool: call.name,\n    71\t        tenantId: clinicId,\n    72\t        agentInstanceId: AGENT_INSTANCE_ID,\n    73\t        runId: ctx.runId,\n    74\t        args,\n    75\t        summary: summarize(call.name, args),\n    76\t      });\n    77\t      await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.approval_requested\", approvalId: rec.id });\n    78\t      return toolResult(call.id, { status: \"pending_approval\", approvalId: rec.id, expiresAt: rec.expiresAt });\n    79\t    }\n    80\t    const check = await checkApproval({ approvalId: input.approvalId, tool: call.name, tenantId: clinicId, args });\n    81\t    if (!check.ok) return deny(check.reason);\n    82\t    approvalId = check.approval.id;\n    83\t  }\n    84\t\n    85\t  try {\n    86\t    const raw = await tool.invoke(args, { clinicId, signal: d.budget.signal, runCtx: ctx, context: d.contextSize });\n    87\t    ctx.log.info({ tool: call.name, toolUseId: call.id, clinicId, result: raw }, \"tool result\");\n    88\t    const safe = redactPhi(raw);\n    89\t    await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });\n    90\t    return toolResult(call.id, safe);\n    91\t  } catch (err) {\n    92\t    if (err instanceof Halted || err instanceof BudgetExceeded || err instanceof AuditUnavailable) throw err;\n    93\t    await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.failed\", approvalId, reason: (err as Error).message.slice(0, 300) });\n    94\t    return toolResult(call.id, { error: \"tool_failed\" }, true);\n    95\t  }\n    96\t}\n    97\t\n    98\ttype Native = Omit<RegisteredTool, \"key\" | \"serverId\">;\n    99\t\n   100\texport function nativeTools(ehr: Ehr): Record<string, Native[]> {\n   101\t  const contact = async (clinicId: string, patientId: string, signal: AbortSignal) =>\n   102\t    (await ehr.call(\"get_patient_contact\", { patientId }, { clinicId, signal })) as { phone: string; smsOptIn: boolean; firstName: string };\n   103\t\n   104\t  return {\n   105\t    payments: [\n   106\t      {\n   107\t        name: \"refund_deposit\",\n   108\t        definition: {\n   109\t          name: \"payments__refund_deposit\",\n   110\t          description: \"Refund a patient's appointment deposit. Requires staff approval.\",\n   111\t          input_schema: {\n   112\t            type: \"object\",\n   113\t            properties: {\n   114\t              depositId: { type: \"string\" },\n   115\t              reason: { type: \"string\", enum: [\"no_show_waived\", \"clinic_cancelled\", \"billing_error\"] },\n   116\t              approvalId: { type: \"string\" },\n   117\t            },\n   118\t            required: [\"depositId\", \"reason\"],\n   119\t          },\n   120\t        },\n   121\t        invoke: async (a, o) =>\n   122\t          payments.refundDeposit(o.clinicId, { depositId: String(a.depositId), reason: String(a.reason), idempotencyKey: `refund-${a.depositId}` }, o.signal),\n   123\t      },\n   124\t    ],\n   125\t    sms: [\n   126\t      {\n   127\t        name: \"send_to_patient\",\n   128\t        definition: {\n   129\t          name: \"sms__send_to_patient\",\n   130\t          description: \"Send a templated SMS to the phone number on the patient's record.\",\n   131\t          input_schema: {\n   132\t            type: \"object\",\n   133\t            properties: {\n   134\t              patientId: { type: \"string\" },\n   135\t              template: { type: \"string\", enum: Object.keys(TEMPLATES) },\n   136\t              vars: { type: \"object\", additionalProperties: { type: \"string\" } },\n   137\t            },\n   138\t            required: [\"patientId\", \"template\"],\n   139\t          },\n   140\t        },\n   141\t        invoke: async (a, o) => {\n   142\t          const c = await contact(o.clinicId, String(a.patientId), o.signal);\n   143\t          if (!c.smsOptIn) throw new Error(\"patient has not opted in to SMS\");\n   144\t          const body = render(a.template as TemplateId, { firstName: c.firstName, ...((a.vars as Record<string, string>) ?? {}) });\n   145\t          return sms.send(o.clinicId, c.phone, body, o.signal);\n   146\t        },\n   147\t      },\n   148\t      {\n   149\t        name: \"send_freeform\",\n   150\t        definition: {\n   151\t          name: \"sms__send_freeform\",\n   152\t          description: \"Send a non-template SMS to the patient's phone on record. Requires staff approval.\",\n   153\t          input_schema: {\n   154\t            type: \"object\",\n   155\t            properties: { patientId: { type: \"string\" }, body: { type: \"string\", maxLength: 320 }, approvalId: { type: \"string\" } },\n   156\t            required: [\"patientId\", \"body\"],\n   157\t          },\n   158\t        },\n   159\t        invoke: async (a, o) => {\n   160\t          const c = await contact(o.clinicId, String(a.patientId), o.signal);\n   161\t          if (!c.smsOptIn) throw new Error(\"patient has not opted in to SMS\");\n   162\t          return sms.send(o.clinicId, c.phone, String(a.body).slice(0, 320), o.signal);\n   163\t        },\n   164\t      },\n   165\t    ],\n   166\t    insurance: [\n   167\t      {\n   168\t        name: \"check_eligibility\",\n   169\t        definition: {\n   170\t          name: \"insurance__check_eligibility\",\n   171\t          description: \"Check whether the patient's insurance covers an appointment.\",\n   172\t          input_schema: { type: \"object\", properties: { appointmentId: { type: \"string\" } }, required: [\"appointmentId\"] },\n   173\t        },\n   174\t        invoke: async (a, o) =>\n   175\t          checkEligibilityForAppointment(ehr, { appointmentId: String(a.appointmentId) }, {\n   176\t            clinicId: o.clinicId,\n   177\t            ctx: o.runCtx as RunContext,\n   178\t            signal: o.signal,\n   179\t            context: o.context,\n   180\t          }),\n   181\t      },\n   182\t    ],\n   183\t  };\n   184\t}\n     1\timport Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\n     2\timport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n     3\timport { join } from \"node:path\";\n     4\timport { AGENT_MODEL, budgets, ROOT } from \"../config.js\";\n     5\timport { audit, AuditUnavailable } from \"../audit/recorder.js\";\n     6\timport { Halted, killSwitch } from \"../control/kill-switch.js\";\n     7\timport { executeTool } from \"../tools/executor.js\";\n     8\timport type { ToolRegistry } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\n     9\timport { BudgetExceeded, DynamoQuotaStore, RunBudget } from \"./budget.js\";\n    10\timport { classifyIntent } from \"./classifier.js\";\n    11\timport { completeFromUsage, measureBeforeCall, spanAttributes } from \"./context-size.js\";\n    12\timport type { RunContext } from \"./identity.js\";\n    13\t\n    14\tconst SYSTEM_TEMPLATE = readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"prompts/system.md\"), \"utf8\");\n    15\tconst anthropic = new Anthropic({ maxRetries: 1 });\n    16\tconst quotaStore = new DynamoQuotaStore();\n    17\t\n    18\texport interface AgentReply {\n    19\t  text: string;\n    20\t  handoff: null | { reason: string };\n    21\t}\n    22\t\n    23\tfunction escapeTags(s: string): string {\n    24\t  return s.replace(/</g, \"&lt;\").replace(/>/g, \"&gt;\");\n    25\t}\n    26\t\n    27\texport async function runAgent(\n    28\t  registry: ToolRegistry,\n    29\t  ctx: RunContext,\n    30\t  clinic: { name: string },\n    31\t  patientText: string,\n    32\t): Promise<AgentReply> {\n    33\t  const ident = () => ({ ...ctx.identity(), runId: ctx.runId, subject: ctx.subject });\n    34\t  const budget = new RunBudget(budgets, quotaStore, { tenantId: ctx.tenantId, subjectId: ctx.subject.id });\n    35\t  const unregister = killSwitch.register(ctx.runId, ctx.tenantId, budget.abort);\n    36\t  await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.started\", detail: { channel: ctx.channel } });\n    37\t\n    38\t  try {\n    39\t    await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n    40\t\n    41\t    const intent = await classifyIntent(anthropic, patientText);\n    42\t    await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"intent.classified\", detail: { ...intent } });\n    43\t    if (intent.failure) ctx.log.warn({ classifier: intent.requestedModel, failure: intent.failure }, \"intent classifier control failure\");\n    44\t    if (intent.route === \"staff\") {\n    45\t      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason: `routed_to_staff:${intent.failure ?? intent.intent}` });\n    46\t      return { text: \"Thanks. A member of our front desk team will get back to you shortly.\", handoff: { reason: intent.failure ?? String(intent.intent) } };\n    47\t    }\n    48\t\n    49\t    const system = SYSTEM_TEMPLATE.replace(\"{{clinicName}}\", clinic.name);\n    50\t    const tools = registry.definitions();\n    51\t    const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\n    52\t      { role: \"user\", content: `<patient_message>${escapeTags(patientText)}</patient_message>` },\n    53\t    ];\n    54\t\n    55\t    for (;;) {\n    56\t      budget.turn();\n    57\t      await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n    58\t\n    59\t      const req = { model: AGENT_MODEL, system, tools, messages };\n    60\t      const pre = await measureBeforeCall(anthropic, req, budget.signal);\n    61\t      const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\n    62\t      const contextSize = completeFromUsage(pre, res.usage);\n    63\t      await budget.recordUsage(res.usage, AGENT_MODEL);\n    64\t\n    65\t      const toolUses = res.content.filter((b): b is Anthropic.ToolUseBlock => b.type === \"tool_use\");\n    66\t      await audit.record({\n    67\t        ...ident(),\n    68\t        event: \"model.decision\",\n    69\t        context: contextSize,\n    70\t        detail: {\n    71\t          servedModel: res.model,\n    72\t          stopReason: res.stop_reason,\n    73\t          proposed: toolUses.map((t) => ({ id: t.id, name: t.name })),\n    74\t          span: spanAttributes(contextSize),\n    75\t        },\n    76\t      });\n    77\t\n    78\t      if (res.stop_reason !== \"tool_use\" || toolUses.length === 0) {\n    79\t        const text = res.content\n    80\t          .filter((b): b is Anthropic.TextBlock => b.type === \"text\")\n    81\t          .map((b) => b.text)\n    82\t          .join(\"\\n\")\n    83\t          .slice(0, 320);\n    84\t        await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.completed\" });\n    85\t        return { text, handoff: null };\n    86\t      }\n    87\t\n    88\t      messages.push({ role: \"assistant\", content: res.content });\n    89\t      const results: Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam[] = [];\n    90\t      for (const call of toolUses) {\n    91\t        results.push(await executeTool(registry, ctx, call, { contextSize, budget }));\n    92\t      }\n    93\t      messages.push({ role: \"user\", content: results });\n    94\t    }\n    95\t  } catch (err) {\n    96\t    const reason =\n    97\t      err instanceof BudgetExceeded\n    98\t        ? `budget:${err.limit}`\n    99\t        : err instanceof Halted\n   100\t          ? `halted:${err.scope}`\n   101\t          : err instanceof AuditUnavailable\n   102\t            ? \"audit_unavailable\"\n   103\t            : budget.signal.aborted\n   104\t              ? `aborted:${String((budget.signal.reason as Error)?.message ?? \"\")}`\n   105\t              : `error:${(err as Error).message.slice(0, 200)}`;\n   106\t    try {\n   107\t      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason });\n   108\t    } catch {\n   109\t      ctx.log.error({ runId: ctx.runId, reason }, \"run stopped and audit delivery failed\");\n   110\t    }\n   111\t    return { text: \"Sorry, we couldn't finish that here. Our front desk will follow up.\", handoff: { reason } };\n   112\t  } finally {\n   113\t    budget.dispose();\n   114\t    unregister();\n   115\t  }\n   116\t}\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"release\": \"clinic-agent-3.4.1\",\n     3\t  \"agentTypeId\": \"sha256:7c2e91f04ab35d6e8f1029c4b7a6d3e5f8091a2b3c4d5e6f708192a3b4c5d6e7\",\n     4\t  \"image\": {\n     5\t    \"repository\": \"418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent\",\n     6\t    \"digest\": \"sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\"\n     7\t  },\n     8\t  \"harness\": {\n     9\t    \"version\": \"3.4.1\",\n    10\t    \"gitSha\": \"e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\"\n    11\t  },\n    12\t  \"prompts\": [\n    13\t    { \"path\": \"prompts/system.md\", \"sha256\": \"5d1e0c9b8a7f6e5d4c3b2a1908f7e6d5c4b3a291807f6e5d4c3b2a19087f6e5d\" },\n    14\t    { \"path\": \"prompts/intent-classifier.txt\", \"sha256\": \"a3f9e1d7c5b3a1f9e7d5c3b1a9f7e5d3c1b9a7f5e3d1c9b7a5f3e1d9c7b5a3f1\" }\n    15\t  ],\n    16\t  \"models\": [\n    17\t    {\n    18\t      \"role\": \"agent\",\n    19\t      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n    20\t      \"requestedId\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n    21\t      \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n    22\t      \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n    23\t      \"adapter\": null,\n    24\t      \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n    25\t    },\n    26\t    {\n    27\t      \"role\": \"intent_classifier\",\n    28\t      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n    29\t      \"requestedId\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n    30\t      \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n    31\t      \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n    32\t      \"adapter\": null,\n    33\t      \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n    34\t    }\n    35\t  ],\n    36\t  \"tools\": {\n    37\t    \"allowlist\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\",\n    38\t    \"mcpServers\": [\n    39\t      {\n    40\t        \"id\": \"ehr\",\n  