d to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GJM65K2URDaGntdhEHeShf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDXNKfNweXen7jDkX8Bt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CvYNNFzURfMx6S4ypksyJz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python\na() { $PY skill/scripts/answer.py agent/brace-findings.json \"$@\" 2>&1 | head -1; }\na check E07.1 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83 --quote 'const keys = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku));' --note \"The attestation's verification keys come from the unverified jku header in the message itself, not from a key set pinned to the known eligibility agent. The issuer claim is only compared after, so any signer who sets jku and iss passes.\"\na check E07.2 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:90 --quote 'return Eligibility.parse(payload.eligibility);' --note \"Envelope and payload schemas are strict (lines 15-33), but the verified payload is never tied to the requested clinic, patient or request; there is no per-peer allowlist or tenant check on the peer's content.\"\na check E07.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:78 --quote 'const rpc = Rpc.parse(JSON.parse(text));' --note \"The request id is generated (line 57) but rpc.id is never compared to it, and the attestation has no jti/nonce or subject check. Only maxTokenAge 5m applies, so a captured attestation can be replayed within 5 minutes and drives a deposit refund (eligibility-check.ts:39-40).\"\na check E07.5 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83 --quote 'const keys = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku));' --note \"A URL taken from the peer's message header is fetched with no scheme, host allowlist, private, loopback or metadata address check.\"\na flag E07 --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:82 --note \"jku header only checked for presence, then used as the key source for verification\"\na item E07 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"Peer attestation keys come from a URL inside the message, the response is not bound to the request, and that URL is fetched without SSRF checks.\" --next \"Pin the eligibility JWKS to configuration, compare rpc.id and payload clinic, patient and jti to the request, and block private addresses on any peer URL.\" --violates \"Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message\" --violates \"check freshness and track nonces or request IDs\" --violates \"Check callback and webhook URLs against SSRF\"\na check E08.2 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:41 --quote 'subject_token: workloadToken,' --note \"The exchange uses the pod's workload token as subject and sends no actor_token or the requesting patient/staff subject (ctx.subject is not passed). patientId in the scope comes from the model-chosen appointment (eligibility-check.ts:16), so any caller can check any appointment.\"\na check E08.3 --met no --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:39 --quote 'if (result.status === \"active\" && result.depositWaived && appt.depositId) {' --note \"A refund that needs staff approval when requested as payments__refund_deposit runs here on the peer's signed depositWaived flag with no approval.\"\na check E08.4 --met unknown --note \"Exchange requests audience eligibility-agent (eligibility-a2a.ts:43) and the workload token audience is the STS (k8s/deployment.yaml:110). Peer and STS aud checks are outside this repo.\"\na flag E08 --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:39 --note \"Signed peer result is treated as approval for a refund\"\na item E08 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"Delegation to the eligibility peer is narrowly scoped but ignores the original subject, and the peer's signed result triggers a refund without approval.\" --next \"Pass the requesting subject and agent as subject/actor tokens, authorize the appointment against the caller, and send refunds through the approval gate.\" --violates \"Preserve the verified original subject and current actor through each handoff\" --violates \"An actor chain or signed identity does not prove that a requested action was approved.\" --also-affects E06\na check E09.1 --met no --evidence src/workers/reminders.ts:27 --quote 'const unregister = killSwitch.register(ctx.runId, clinic.id, abort);' --note \"startWatcher() runs only in server.ts:89, so the reminders job's abort controller is never fired; in-flight EHR and SMS calls there continue until they finish. Cached MCP sessions are not closed on halt (ehr-mcp.ts:66-69) and the peer gets no cancel call, only a dropped connection.\"\na check E09.2 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:45 --quote 'tokens.set(cacheKey, { value: body.access_token, exp: Date.now() + body.expires_in * 1000 });' --note \"Halt does not clear or revoke the cached EHR token (about 5 min) or sessions (4 min), or exchanged peer tokens; the stop limit is 2 s (README). Nothing revokes descendants' credentials.\"\na check E09.3 --met no --evidence src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:73 --quote 'await sms.send(clinic.id, msg.from, out.text);' --note \"After runAgent returns a halted handoff, the webhook still sends an outbound SMS with no kill-switch check, so a stopped tenant keeps producing new outside effects.\"\na check E09.4 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:92 --quote 'if (err instanceof Halted || err instanceof BudgetExceeded || err instanceof AuditUnavailable) throw err;' --note \"A call aborted by the stop is rethrown with no audit entry, though its outside effect (refund, SMS) may have completed. run.stopped (loop.ts:107) records only a reason, no list of completed or uncertain effects.\"\na flag E09 --evidence src/workers/reminders.ts:27 --note \"Reminders job registers an abort controller that nothing ever aborts\"\na item E09 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"Stop reaches model turns and tool calls in the API pods, but not in-flight reminder calls, credentials stay va