ed sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83\",\n          \"quote\": \"const keys = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku));\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The attestation's verification keys come from the unverified jku header in the message itself, not from a key set pinned to the known eligibility agent. The issuer claim is only compared after, so any signer who sets jku and iss passes.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E07.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Message types and schemas are validated, and each request is checked against what that peer is allowed to ask for, including tenant.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open the peer message handler. 2) Check message type and schema validation. 3) Check a per-peer allowlist of request types and tenants, keyed on the authenticated sender. 4) Answer no if schemas are unchecked, any authenticated peer can ask for anything, or tenant is taken from the message body.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:90\",\n          \"quote\": \"return Eligibility.parse(payload.eligibility);\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Envelope and payload schemas are strict (lines 15-33), but the verified payload is never tied to the requested clinic, patient or request; there is no per-peer allowlist or tenant check on the peer's content.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E07.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Action requests carry a nonce or request ID and a freshness check, and replays are rejected or do not repeat side effects.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find action request handling. 2) Check for 