    \"problem\": \"A tool's description or schema changing after it was approved\",\n          \"owner\": \"E03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Peer agent identity not authenticated on each message\",\n          \"owner\": \"E07\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Gateway not authenticating callers or authorizing each action\",\n          \"owner\": \"E06\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/tools/registry.ts\",\n          \"line\": 128,\n          \"note\": \"Key is manifest server id plus tool name; id is bound to a pinned URL and TLS fingerprint.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E05.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Tools are keyed by verified server identity (endpoint, credential, or registry namespace) plus tool name, never by bare tool name or a server's self-reported name.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the tool registry or lookup map. 2) Check its key is a verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace plus tool name. 3) Answer no if tools are keyed by bare tool name or the server's self-reported name (`serverInfo.name`), or a later server overwrites an earlier entry with the same tool name.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:128\",\n          \"quote\": \"key: `${serverId}__${t.name}`,\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src for serverInfo.name, getServerVersion and bare-name lookups; reportedName (ehr-mcp.ts:83) only reaches the rejection log at registry.ts:109. add() rejects repeated keys (registry.ts:138), so no later server overwrites an entry.\",\n          \"note\": \"Key is manifest server id plus tool name; id is bound to a pinned URL and TLS fingerprint.\",\n          \"coverage\": [\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"I131c91d8de\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:128\",\n              \"quote\": \"key: `${serverId}__${t.name}`,\",\n              \"note\": \"MCP tools are registered under the manifest server id plus tool name; reportedName is not used in the key.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"I18aec0bd94\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:94\",\n              \"quote\": \"for (const t of tools) this.add({ ...t, serverId, key: `${serverId}__${t.name}` });\",\n              \"note\": \"Native tools use the fixed namespace (payments, sms, insurance) plus tool name.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"I140bd2f97f\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:107\",\n              \"quote\": \"const cfg = this.servers.find((s) => s.id === serverId);\",\n              \"note\": \"registerMcp refuses any serverId that is not a release-manifest server.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"I1861b59462\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/server.ts:49\",\n              \"quote\": \"registry.registerMcp(\\\"ehr\\\", reportedName, meta, (tool, input, opts) => ehr.call(tool, input, opts));\",\n              \"note\": \"The only MCP registration passes the literal manifest id 'ehr' for the pinned client; reportedName is informational.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"ehr connection identity\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:22\",\n              \"quote\": \"return got === expected ? undefined : new Error(`EHR MCP certificate mismatch: ${got}`);\",\n              \"note\": \"Server identity is the pinned manifest URL and TLS certificate fingerprint.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"registry overwrite\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:138\",\n              \"quote\": \"if (this.tools.has(t.key)) {\",\n              \"note\": \"A repeated key is rejected and flagged rather than overwriting the earlier entry.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"executor lookup\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:56\",\n              \"quote\": \"const tool = registry.get(call.name);\",\n              \"note\": \"Lookup is by the namespaced key only.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"src/workers/reminders.ts\",\n              \"status\": \"not_applicable\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/workers/reminders.ts:21\",\n              \"quote\": \"const ehr = ehrClient(manifest.tools.mcpServers.find((s: { id: string }) => s.id === \\\"ehr\\\"));\",\n              \"note\": \"The cron job calls fixed EHR tool names in code with the manifest server; it has no model-visible tool registry.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E05.2\",\n          \"check\": \"The registry flags duplicate and lookalike tool names across servers.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Trace name comparison across servers. 2) Construct repeated confusable substitutions, multiple edits and normalization-boundary examples, starting from an existing tool name; record canonical outputs, comparison result and registration outcome. 3) Answer no if a duplicate or demonstrated lookalike is accepted without a conflict flag. The existence of normalization/edit-distance code is insufficient; namespacing and approval binding do not satisfy this separate check.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:151\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (editDistanceAtMostOne(canonical(existing.name), c)) {\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Lookalike test allows one edit after canonicalization. Tool names must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}$ (metadata-scan.ts:121). Second server tool check_el1g1b1l1ty canonicalizes to ellglblllty-form 'checkellglblllty' vs 'checkeligibility' (1 maps to l, never i): 4 edits, not equal, distance>1, so it registers with no conflict flag. Same for list_patient_appointments -> l1st_patient_appo1ntments (2 edits). Existing duplicate/one-edit cases are flagged (controls.test.ts).\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E05.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Approval is bound to the verified server identity, so a new server with a matching tool name or self-reported name does not inherit approval or replace the approved tool.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where tool approval is stored and checked. 2) Check approval is keyed by verified server identity, not tool name or self-reported server name. 3) Answer no if a new server with a matching tool name or server name would count as approved or replace the approved tool.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/approvals.ts:75\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \\\"approval is for a different tool\\\" };\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched approvals.ts and executor.ts for lookups by bare tool name or reported server name; the approval stores and compares call.name (the namespaced key). Other approval fields (argsHash) are B06 scope.\",\n          \"note\": \"Approval and allowlist are keyed by the namespaced key, so a new server id does not inherit approval.\",\n          \"coverage\": [\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"allowlist\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:55\",\n              \"quote\": \"if (!ALLOWED.has(call.name)) return deny(\\\"not_allowlisted\\\");\",\n              \"note\": \"Allowlist entries are namespaced keys such as ehr__cancel_appointment, so a tool from a new server id is not allowed.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"approval request\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:70\",\n              \"quote\": \"tool: call.name,\",\n              \"note\": \"The approval record stores the namespaced key, including the server id.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"approval check\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/approvals.ts:75\",\n              \"quote\": \"if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \\\"approval is for a different tool\\\" };\",\n              \"note\": \"An approval for ehr__x does not satisfy ehr2__x or payments__x.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"high-impact policy\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:67\",\n              \"quote\": \"if (policy.highImpactTools.includes(call.name)) {\",\n              \"note\": \"High-impact list is keyed by the namespaced name.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"subject\": \"replacement\",\n              \"status\": \"enforced\",\n              \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:148\",\n              \"quote\": \"this.rejected.push({ serverId: t.serverId, tool: t.name, reason: `same bare name as ${existing.key}` });\",\n              \"note\": \"A second server with the same bare name is rejected and cannot replace the approved tool.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"Flag lookalike and duplicate names across servers.\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Tools are namespaced and duplicates are flagged, but the lookalike test only catches one edit after canonicalization, so multi-confusable names register unflagged.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Compare canonical names with a length-scaled edit distance and map 1 to both i and l; add tests for repeated confusables and multi-edit names.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"E06\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Enforced gateway boundary\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Send MCP calls through a gateway or equivalent enforcement layer the agent cannot bypass. Choose controls for internal HTTP servers, public third-party services, and local stdio servers; private networking and mTLS are one internal deployment pattern, not universal MCP requirements. Authenticate each caller, preserve agent and delegated-subject identity, and authorize each action's tool, operation, resource, tenant, and arguments. Apply the same policy to direct calls, dynamic tools, CLI/code mode, and wrappers. Validate calls and responses, enforce rate limits, and log every decision. For HTTP OAuth, validate access tokens for the gateway's own audience, issuer, expiry, and scopes; obtain separately authorized backend credentials through a trusted issuer or supported exchange. Never accept a token for another resource or relay it unchanged as a substitute for backend authorization. Keep backend secrets and tokens away from agent-controlled execution paths. Restrict local process launch, files, environment, credentials, and network in the host or sandbox. Under MCP 2026-07-28, reject metadata-header/body mismatches before routing or policy relies on them. Isolate private caches by verified authorization context, tenant, resource, and policy version; share only data explicitly approved as public. Authorize explicit task/state handles on every operation; neither a connection nor self-reported metadata establishes identity. Where the gateway is an OAuth client, validate authorization-server issuer responses and protect discovery URLs against SSRF. Record protocol and extension versions and test each enabled extension's boundary, including task access/cancellation and MCP Apps sandbox, CSP, bridge messages, and UI-initiated tool authorization. Test bypass, cross-tenant access, malformed traffic, and required-check outages. Required checks fail closed.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Tool inventory missing a task-based reason for each tool\",\n          \"owner\": \"B01\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent credential granting wildcard or admin permissions\",\n          \"owner\": \"B02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Destructive actions running without a higher-authority approval\",\n          \"owner\": \"B05\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Hidden instructions inside a tool's metadata\",\n          \"owner\": \"E04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Outbound traffic to unapproved internet destinations\",\n          \"owner\": \"B09\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts\",\n          \"line\": 58,\n          \"note\": \"EHR gets a clinic-level client_credentials token with fixed read+write scopes (ehr-mcp.ts:41,49) for every call. The acting patient or staff subject and agent identity are not passed; only x-clinic-id. Scope is not narrowed per tool.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Every governed tool path uses an enforced boundary suited to its internal HTTP, public third-party, or local stdio deployment; agent-controlled code cannot bypass it or obtain backend credentials.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Inventory HTTP, dynamic, CLI/code-mode, wrapper and local-process paths. 2) Trace effective egress, backend credential custody and process/file/env/network restrictions. 3) Internal private networking/mTLS is one option; public services can use agent-side egress and broker-held credentials. 4) Reject any usable unmediated path; do not require operator control of a public provider's network. Use unknown for enforcement outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Looked at executor.ts, registry.ts, ehr-mcp.ts and k8s/deployment.yaml:159-195. All model tool calls go through executeTool and a NetworkPolicy limits egress to DNS, the EHR CIDR and the platform proxy. The proxy allowlist is platform-owned and only described in a comment (k8s:160-161), and the wrapper path in eligibility-check.ts:40 is filed under E06.3.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06.2\",\n          \"check\": \"The gateway validates its own incoming token audience, issuer, expiry and scopes, and obtains separately authorized, backend-specific credentials while preserving agent and delegated-subject identity.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Trace client-to-gateway and gateway-to-backend credentials independently. 2) Check trusted issuer, audience, grants, expiry and supported exchange/grant. 3) Reject tokens meant for other resources or unchanged incoming-token forwarding used instead of backend authorization. 4) A scoped delegated-user token is valid when the acting agent is verified separately; a vault alone does not create expiring tokens.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:58\",\n          \"quote\": \"headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, \\\"x-clinic-id\\\": clinicId },\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"EHR gets a clinic-level client_credentials token with fixed read+write scopes (ehr-mcp.ts:41,49) for every call. The acting patient or staff subject and agent identity are not passed; only x-clinic-id. Scope is not narrowed per tool.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Every direct, dynamic, CLI/code-mode and wrapper call receives action/resource/tenant/argument authorization, request/response validation, rate limits and decision logging.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Enumerate every execution path, not only tools/call. 2) Trace the same authorization, validation, quota and logging policy in each. 3) Reject alternate paths that invoke a disabled or denied tool, authorize only a tool name, or change tenant/resource authority. Use unknown for unavailable implementation evidence.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:63\",\n          \"quote\": \"const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \\\"string\\\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Tenant for the call comes from model-supplied input.clinicId for any subject (patients included), with no check against the subject's clinic or role. No request schema or response validation runs in executeTool. insurance__check_eligibility wrapper also calls payments.refundDeposit (eligibility-check.ts:40) without the highImpact approval gate.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06.4\",\n          \"check\": \"If a required check (policy engine, scanner, token check) errors or times out, the call is blocked.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the policy engine, scanner, and token check. 2) Check each error blocks the call. 3) Answer no if any error branch allows the call or logs and continues, or a config flag defaults to fail-open.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:52\",\n          \"quote\": \"req.log.warn({ err: (err as Error).message }, \\\"sms webhook signature check failed\\\");\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"A failed or erroring signature check is logged and counted, then the handler goes on to parse the body and run the agent. Kill switch, approval store, scanner and audit paths do fail closed.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06.5\",\n          \"check\": \"Under MCP 2026-07-28, relevant header/body mismatches are rejected before routing or policy relies on them, and private caches/state/task handles are isolated by verified authorization context, tenant, resource and policy version.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Identify supported protocol versions. 2) For 2026-07-28, trace version/method/name/parameter header validation before affected routing/policy decisions. 3) Trace cache keys/invalidation and every task/state-handle operation, including status/results and cancellation where present. 4) Reject cross-tenant/caller reads or stale grants after revocation; permit shared cache entries only when explicitly public. 5) Do not require removed protocol sessions for 2026-07-28; test legacy session binding only when that version is enabled.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Looked in ehr-mcp.ts, registry.ts and package.json (MCP SDK 1.18.2). No supported protocol version is recorded, no task or state handles exist, and the token/session caches are keyed by clinic id (ehr-mcp.ts:33,53). Header/body checks live in the SDK or server, outside this repo.\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06.6\",\n          \"check\": \"If the gateway is itself an OAuth client, it checks the authorization server's issuer (iss, RFC 9207) and blocks private and metadata addresses in discovery URLs. Answer yes with the code line, or yes citing the config that shows it isn't an OAuth client.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Check whether the gateway acts as an OAuth client (gets tokens, follows discovery or metadata URLs). 2) If so, check RFC 9207 issuer-response comparison and rejection when an advertised required iss is missing; do not require an absent iss when the selected protocol permits it. Check it blocks unauthorized private, loopback, and metadata destinations, including on redirects and DNS resolution. Explicitly approved internal issuer endpoints may be allowed by trusted configuration; untrusted discovery must not widen that allowlist. 3) Answer no if either is missing. If it is not an OAuth client, answer yes citing the config that shows that.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Looked at ehr-mcp.ts:36-46 and eligibility-a2a.ts:35-50. Client-credentials token_url comes from Secrets Manager and the exchange URL from env; no discovery or authorization-response flow exists, but eligibility-a2a.ts:83 fetches a peer-supplied jku URL with no private-address check (filed under E07.5).\",\n          \"coverage\": [],\n          \"deviations\": [],\n          \"attempts\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06.7\",\n          \"check\": \"Enabled MCP extensions have recorded versions and enforced boundaries, including Tasks ownership/cancellation and Apps sandbox/CSP/bridge/tool-call authorization where present.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Inventory enabled extensions and versions from client/server/host configuration. 2) Trace extension-specific authorization, task ownership/status/results/cancellation, and Apps host sandbox, CSP, bridge-message validation and UI-triggered tool policy. 3) Reject a bypass or missing require