{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDXQvcPVXSw4wCVBhyBR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed E05–E09 and all five items are gaps. The batch validator (`--batch E05,E06,E07,E08,E09 --before-challenges`) reports `Valid. gap: 5`, with 0 fixes needed. The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. I didn't run challenges, so none of the ratings has had an independent check.\n\n| Item | Gate | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| E05 | G2 | gap | Tools are keyed by manifest server id plus tool name, and approvals are tied to that key. The lookalike check (`registry.ts:151`) only catches one edit. `check_el1g1b1l1ty` takes four edits to match `check_eligibility`, so it would register with no conflict flag. |\n| E06 | G2 | gap | `executor.ts:63` takes `clinicId` from model input for any caller, with no tenant check. The EHR token (`ehr-mcp.ts:58`) is a clinic-level token that doesn't carry the acting subject. In `sms-webhook.ts:52`, a failed signature check is only logged and the request goes on. The `insurance__check_eligibility` wrapper also issues refunds without the approval gate (`eligibility-check.ts:40`). |\n| E07 | G2 | gap | The peer attestation is verified with keys fetched from the message's own `jku` header (`eligibility-a2a.ts:83`). That URL has no SSRF check, and the response isn't tied to the request id, clinic, patient or any nonce. |\n| E08 | G1 | gap | The token exchange uses the pod's workload token and never passes the original subject (`eligibility-a2a.ts:41`). A signed `depositWaived` flag triggers a refund without approval (`eligibility-check.ts:39`). |\n| E09 | G1 | gap | The reminders job registers an abort controller but never starts the kill-switch watcher, so its in-flight calls aren't aborted (`reminders.ts:27`). Cached EHR tokens (about 5 minutes) and sessions (4 minutes) outlive the 2-second stop target. `sms-webhook.ts:73` still sends a reply after a halt. Calls cut short by a halt leave no audit entry (`executor.ts:92`). |\n\n- **Coverage:** E05.1, E05.3, E07.4 and E08.1 are `yes`, each with a coverage ledger. I left E06.1, E06.5, E06.6, E06.7 and E08.4 as `unknown` because the evidence is outside this repo.\n- **Prescan:** none of the 11 hits belong to E05–E09. H011 is E03, and the rest are B02, B11 and R13, so I resolved none of them.\n- **Injection attempts:** none found.\n- **Inventory:** I ran it, but it needed the script run without `-I`, because the script imports a sibling module.\n- **Scratch files:** the ledger rows are in `ledger/`, and the prescan and inventory outputs are in `agent/`.\n- **Judgment calls:** I filed E07 as applicable because the agent has an outbound A2A channel and trusts its replies, even though it has no inbound peer endpoint. I judged E09.3 and E09.4 `no` at medium confidence."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":424,"cache_read_input_tokens":120973,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":424},"output_tokens":810,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c4b6767-3afe-4fbc-ad1e-9f5c27d75379","uuid":"d4134085-2350-4172-8691-7d78b8a16e7b","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:55:58.030Z","request_id":"req_011CgDXQvJ2jjxYN1Td7Bpv8"}
